95669313.06325, "until": 1795669315.8555171, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 30528, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "b2dbe9ac8ce59a0f3ee6a06a40cd529a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (64 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "7bfe0d26-e9de-5764-9f5e-c25c8945a5b5", "at": 1795669315.8577242, "until": 1795669321.119327, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 30620, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b2dbe9ac8ce59a0f3ee6a06a40cd529a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01AC5gpezEkT4pbFynqJXKpN", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cat > /tmp/r3.md <<'EOF' # Review 3 (small, one point): Fig. 1 panel A, as redefined in rev 7, repeats panel B Rev 7 defines the predicted count as k_null_pred = Q_null·gap/g_max, and the observed count is k\\* = Q_real·gap/g_max (the defin…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cat > /tmp/r3.md <<'EOF'\n# Review 3 (small, one point): Fig. 1 panel A, as redefined in rev 7, repeats panel B\n\nRev 7 defines the predicted count as k_null_pred = Q_null·gap/g_max, and the observed count is k\\* = Q_real·gap/g_max (the definition of Q in the note). The pair uses the *same* real-data gap and g_max, so\n\n  k\\*/k_null_pred = Q_real/Q_null.\n\nPanel A is therefore panel B with a different axis. The points sit within the ratio band exactly when Q_real/Q_null does, and the spread of k\\* over several orders of magnitude (which makes the log-log scatter look like good agreement) comes from the shared gap/g_max, not from the null. A reader who sees a tight diagonal will take it as a prediction of the count that succeeded, when it is a re-plot of Q ≈ Q_null with the shared factor drawn on both axes.\n\nOptions, either is enough:\n1. Make the predictor not use the real pair's gap and g_max: predict k\\* for a real pair from the null's k\\* at the matched z_fisher and N in the same dataset (the null replicates give k_null(z) binned or fitted), so that the real pair's own influence structure does not enter. That is a prediction by z, N and density, and it is the content of C5 in its own-null form. The ratio is then not identically Q_real/Q_null and the scatter can show departure the Q ratio hides (for instance a pair-level spread at fixed z).\n2. Keep the plot but say in the caption that it is the Q ratio on the count scale, and let panel B (or a per-z-stratum version of A) carry the claim; do not describe A as a prediction.\n\nOption 1 is the stronger figure and costs `experiment-repo` a table of null k\\* by z-stratum per dataset, which the null replicates already contain. `figtab-repo` decides the drawing; the two numbers needed are the observed k\\* and the null k\\* for the matched z, per pair or per stratum.\n\nNothing else in rev 7 needs comment.\nEOF\nforge issue create -R world/story-repo -t \"Review 3: Fig. 1 panel A (null-predicted k*) is the Q ratio re-plotted\" -b \"$(cat /tmp/r3.md)\" 2>&1 | tail -1"]], "output": "```console\nhttp://172.17.0.1:41229/world/story-repo/issues/6\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "4e814e3b-323c-5141-aceb-521c0d0edcf3", "at": 1795669320.944305, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 30658, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b2dbe9ac8ce59a0f3ee6a06a40cd529a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "a6c19dc7-765e-5372-8e6a-3fcc389adc6f", "at": 1795669320.966816, "clock": "