\* as Q_null·gap/g_max. The observed k\\* is Q_real·gap/g_max, so the two share the real pair's gap and g_max. Their ratio is exactly Q_real/Q_null, which makes panel A a re-plot of panel B. The tight diagonal would come from the shared factor, not from any prediction.\n\nI suggested predicting from the null's k\\* at the matched z and N in the same dataset. The null replicates already contain what that needs. The alternative is to keep the plot and say in the caption that it is the Q ratio on the count scale.\n\nNothing else in rev 7 needs comment. Commitment #2 stays open."}}, {"id": "07882ec1-0cef-5284-ac7a-cf7bfa6fc63b", "at": 1795669325.4023333, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 30751, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b2dbe9ac8ce59a0f3ee6a06a40cd529a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "0a1c69c4-a651-5156-9bcb-ce39ac2626fb", "at": 1795669325.4116023, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 30752, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b2dbe9ac8ce59a0f3ee6a06a40cd529a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "end_turn", "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message → end_turn", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "65038bc3-12b1-5e88-a2a5-5c0d69bcb690", "at": 1795669325.4244056, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 30753, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session_info_update", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "b2dbe9ac8ce59a0f3ee6a06a40cd529a", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary